WEBVTT

00:00:01.651 --> 00:00:02.452
On the 9th of this month, ISDA flight 029,

00:00:02.452 --> 00:00:05.322
On the 9th of this month, ISDA flight 029,

00:00:05.322 --> 00:00:05.822
which took off from Sorajima
International Spaceport,

00:00:05.822 --> 00:00:07.691
which took off from Sorajima
International Spaceport,

00:00:07.691 --> 00:00:10.126
exploded in midair,
immediately after takeoff.

00:00:10.126 --> 00:00:13.864
48 passengers and crew
died in the accident.

00:00:13.864 --> 00:00:16.900
The government appointed an
accident investigation commission,

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.002
and conducted an investigation of
the recovered shuttle fragments

00:00:19.002 --> 00:00:22.038
to determine the cause of the accident.

00:00:22.038 --> 00:00:25.542
Additionally, and miraculously,
there was a single passenger,

00:00:25.542 --> 00:00:28.807
Kamishina Jin-san,
who escaped with his life...

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.786
So this... is the Atrum...

00:01:51.127 --> 00:01:56.833
Osanai hi ni nakushita

00:01:56.833 --> 00:02:02.739
sono itami no imi sae

00:02:02.739 --> 00:02:08.478
Uzumakumatte takushita

00:02:08.478 --> 00:02:11.675
Boku wa kitto...

00:02:13.083 --> 00:02:19.422
Ao no hate ni mita yokan wo toraete

00:02:19.422 --> 00:02:26.930
kaze ni nori hikari no sasu hou e

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.799
I'll always be with you

00:02:29.799 --> 00:02:32.435
see the sky in front of you

00:02:32.435 --> 00:02:36.804
fly high in a light from the deepest blue

00:02:38.508 --> 00:02:43.980
Uzumaku hoshi no hibiki ni nosete

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:46.649
utau yo

00:02:46.649 --> 00:02:55.318
Kono koe ga kimi ni todokimasu you ni

00:03:32.595 --> 00:03:34.831
Where am I?

00:03:34.831 --> 00:03:37.823
Farewell, Jin.

00:03:39.536 --> 00:03:41.527
Hold on, Toa!

00:03:46.076 --> 00:03:47.703
Toa!

00:03:54.117 --> 00:03:55.846
Is that?

00:04:05.061 --> 00:04:07.256
Let's go, Gio.

00:04:09.065 --> 00:04:10.760
Gio...

00:04:18.641 --> 00:04:22.979
He never said very much,
but we got along unusually well.

00:04:22.979 --> 00:04:27.150
I really did think of Spirytus as a brother.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:31.143
And now, I've killed him.

00:04:32.922 --> 00:04:36.726
It's not your fault, Howl. I mean,

00:04:36.726 --> 00:04:39.627
when Akira-chan told me to kill him...

00:04:41.464 --> 00:04:44.467
A Master's command is absolute.

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:49.005
That much is established
from the moment of Resonance.

00:04:49.005 --> 00:04:51.241
I'd never give the order to kill anyone.

00:04:51.241 --> 00:04:55.111
Yeah, but for that matter,
how did it come to this?

00:04:55.111 --> 00:04:59.349
Why would Spirytus do what he did?
Was it because of Amagi?

00:04:59.349 --> 00:05:03.479
The ISDA's investigation office
is moving on that right now.

00:05:07.657 --> 00:05:09.625
We didn't have any other choice.

00:05:11.427 --> 00:05:15.365
I'm sorry, Howling Star.

00:05:15.365 --> 00:05:17.967
What we should be doing now

00:05:17.967 --> 00:05:22.005
is finding Kamishina Jin
and Gio as quickly as possible.

00:05:22.005 --> 00:05:24.667
We cannot allow this
disturbance to get any worse.

00:05:30.146 --> 00:05:34.810
Gio... why did you go with Jin?

00:05:43.326 --> 00:05:46.853
Why? Why did you do it?!

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:02.345
You're certain of this?

00:06:02.345 --> 00:06:07.217
For better or worse, one of
the outsiders came around.

00:06:07.217 --> 00:06:11.054
When I showed him a photo of Spirytus,
he said he was certain of it.

00:06:11.054 --> 00:06:15.225
It's unthinkable that a Communicator
would be a mass murderer.

00:06:15.225 --> 00:06:17.894
How could this happen?

00:06:17.894 --> 00:06:21.264
Please, keep looking into this.

00:06:21.264 --> 00:06:22.891
Understood.

00:06:49.892 --> 00:06:55.031
The Dragonauts are frantically
searching for Kamishina Jin and Gio.

00:06:55.031 --> 00:06:58.067
I wish they'd look for the Album, as well.

00:06:58.067 --> 00:07:01.304
Kamishina Jin is the bait to catch her.

00:07:01.304 --> 00:07:04.073
Whatever that's worth, at this point.

00:07:04.073 --> 00:07:07.877
Have you heard anything about Spirytus?

00:07:07.877 --> 00:07:14.484
Mister Cyril believes that the
press must not find out about this.

00:07:14.484 --> 00:07:16.286
In that case...

00:07:16.286 --> 00:07:19.989
There is only one path for us to choose.

00:07:19.989 --> 00:07:24.294
Going public with the truth
about D Project is not possible.

00:07:24.294 --> 00:07:28.631
Telling mankind that they are at
peril from extraterrestrial creatures

00:07:28.631 --> 00:07:31.467
would only arouse unproductive anxiety.

00:07:31.467 --> 00:07:33.736
But the people are already shaken up

00:07:33.736 --> 00:07:36.439
after the events of last night, aren't they?

00:07:36.439 --> 00:07:39.175
The issue at hand is the people
learning that the government

00:07:39.175 --> 00:07:43.513
has authorized the secret
nurturing of Dragons, isn't it?

00:07:43.513 --> 00:07:45.315
You're raising that now?

00:07:45.315 --> 00:07:50.620
Many people have already witnessed
Dragonauts riding their Dragons!

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:51.454
Yes, but...

00:07:51.454 --> 00:07:56.025
Commander Sakaki, what do you think?

00:07:56.025 --> 00:07:59.153
I'd like to hear your thoughts.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.599
If we're going to conceal the identity

00:08:03.599 --> 00:08:07.370
of the culprit behind the string of murders...

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:09.972
...then to divert the
people's awareness away,

00:08:09.972 --> 00:08:13.669
I think we should go public with D Project.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:19.975
I agree.

00:08:29.125 --> 00:08:32.862
What's with the clothes?

00:08:32.862 --> 00:08:36.559
This is what people do, right?

00:08:45.408 --> 00:08:49.712
What are you to Toa?

00:08:49.712 --> 00:08:53.049
I was born to protect Toa.

00:08:53.049 --> 00:08:55.385
Protect Toa?

00:08:55.385 --> 00:08:58.054
What are you to Toa?

00:08:58.054 --> 00:09:01.649
Me? I'm...

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:07.660
What am I to Toa?

00:09:21.778 --> 00:09:23.712
That singing...

00:09:29.118 --> 00:09:32.952
It's Toa. I can hear her.

00:09:36.092 --> 00:09:38.194
You hear something?

00:09:38.194 --> 00:09:40.924
Don't you hear it?

00:09:45.902 --> 00:09:49.305
The Moon. Toa is on the Moon.

00:09:49.305 --> 00:09:51.136
The Moon?

00:09:57.914 --> 00:10:00.883
How do you know that?

00:10:00.883 --> 00:10:03.786
I can hear her song.

00:10:03.786 --> 00:10:05.754
Her song?

00:10:34.283 --> 00:10:36.751
Say, Machina...

00:10:39.789 --> 00:10:42.291
About what was said earlier,

00:10:42.291 --> 00:10:45.528
I wouldn't tell you to kill
anyone, either, Machina.

00:10:45.528 --> 00:10:48.431
There's no way I'd say that.

00:10:48.431 --> 00:10:50.956
Mm-hmm, I know.

00:10:59.775 --> 00:11:01.606
What?!

00:11:02.712 --> 00:11:03.846
Gio!

00:11:03.846 --> 00:11:05.047
That's him?

00:11:05.047 --> 00:11:08.451
Let go! Let me go!

00:11:08.451 --> 00:11:11.487
Kamishina Jin, and the
Communicator, Gio, right?

00:11:11.487 --> 00:11:13.114
That's right.

00:11:14.857 --> 00:11:17.360
I was just being used by this guy.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:22.559
You backstabber! Don't you...
don't you want to see Toa?!

00:11:35.044 --> 00:11:37.246
We've caught the fugitive Kamishina Jin

00:11:37.246 --> 00:11:40.249
and the Communicator, Gio.

00:11:40.249 --> 00:11:43.686
Repeat, we've caught
the fugitive Kamishina Jin

00:11:43.686 --> 00:11:46.689
and the Communicator, Gio.

00:11:46.689 --> 00:11:47.990
Gio!

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:49.859
Lucky you, Kazuki-kun.

00:11:49.859 --> 00:11:53.396
That's one task taken care of.

00:11:53.396 --> 00:11:56.499
So, you heard the voice
of the Album calling you,

00:11:56.499 --> 00:12:00.202
and you don't remember
much after that, then?

00:12:00.202 --> 00:12:01.692
Yeah.

00:12:04.407 --> 00:12:07.043
Take him to Dr. Kitajima.

00:12:07.043 --> 00:12:08.567
Yes, sir.

00:12:11.781 --> 00:12:13.408
Here.

00:12:19.121 --> 00:12:21.555
Don't be shy, drink up.

00:12:25.027 --> 00:12:27.263
Tell me,

00:12:27.263 --> 00:12:30.800
what did you do something so reckless for?

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:35.032
To see Toa. That's all.

00:12:39.041 --> 00:12:42.111
- What's the matter?
- Keep walking!

00:12:42.111 --> 00:12:44.875
Hey, we told you to keep walking.

00:12:52.455 --> 00:12:58.761
What am I to Toa? I want to
go see Toa, to find that out.

00:12:58.761 --> 00:13:02.288
She's the one who told me I'm not alone.

00:13:17.513 --> 00:13:19.415
Intruder in Area D3!

00:13:19.415 --> 00:13:21.610
Bringing up surveillance monitor imaging.

00:13:31.794 --> 00:13:34.922
What the hell has Gio done this time?!

00:13:37.667 --> 00:13:40.136
Don't tell me...

00:13:40.136 --> 00:13:43.606
Don't tell me they've been
working together from the start!

00:13:43.606 --> 00:13:45.608
Akira-chan, what's the matter?

00:13:45.608 --> 00:13:48.044
Machina, you go ahead! Go stop Gio!

00:13:48.044 --> 00:13:49.602
All right.

00:13:57.153 --> 00:13:59.321
Damn, they got us.

00:13:59.321 --> 00:14:00.982
Hold it!

00:14:02.692 --> 00:14:04.994
The Moon?

00:14:04.994 --> 00:14:07.897
How do you know that?

00:14:07.897 --> 00:14:10.866
I can hear her song.

00:14:10.866 --> 00:14:12.527
Her song?

00:14:17.573 --> 00:14:19.875
I don't hear anything.

00:14:19.875 --> 00:14:23.333
Trust me, Toa is on the Moon.

00:14:25.081 --> 00:14:28.244
It's the truth. I can tell.

00:14:29.719 --> 00:14:33.322
If she isn't on the Moon...

00:14:33.322 --> 00:14:36.926
...then this is over. I'm leaving you behind.

00:14:36.926 --> 00:14:39.394
Yeah, fair enough.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:46.068
Let's go.

00:14:46.068 --> 00:14:48.537
Hold on a minute.

00:14:48.537 --> 00:14:53.236
If we're going into space, I need
some things. We have to go get them.

00:14:56.712 --> 00:14:58.509
Open up.

00:15:03.786 --> 00:15:05.344
All right!

00:15:08.891 --> 00:15:10.415
Freeze!

00:15:15.131 --> 00:15:18.123
End of the line, Kamishina Jin.

00:15:32.281 --> 00:15:33.908
You won't get away.

00:15:35.217 --> 00:15:37.920
Okay, let's pick up where we left off.

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:40.556
I still have a whole heap
of questions to ask you.

00:15:40.556 --> 00:15:42.725
Please, let me go.

00:15:42.725 --> 00:15:45.661
How come you, someone
who isn't even a Master,

00:15:45.661 --> 00:15:47.897
was able to ride Gio, a Dragon?

00:15:47.897 --> 00:15:49.899
You haven't even gone through Resonance.

00:15:49.899 --> 00:15:53.068
What are you talking about?
What does that mean?

00:15:53.068 --> 00:15:56.572
Don't play dumb! Answer the question!

00:15:56.572 --> 00:16:00.743
Masters? Resonance? What on
earth are you talking about?

00:16:00.743 --> 00:16:02.111
I told you, don't play dumb!

00:16:02.111 --> 00:16:06.482
I'm not playing dumb! I'd like
to answer you, but I don't know!

00:16:06.482 --> 00:16:09.819
What exactly is this?!
What's going on here?!

00:16:09.819 --> 00:16:13.118
That's what I want to know! Tell me!

00:16:15.024 --> 00:16:17.860
Does he really not know anything?

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:20.988
Then what is there between him and Gio?

00:16:37.179 --> 00:16:40.549
I want to know the truth!
That's why I'm going to go see Toa.

00:16:40.549 --> 00:16:42.540
See her, and find out for sure!

00:16:53.062 --> 00:16:54.552
Hold it!

00:17:23.492 --> 00:17:25.551
You won't get away from me!

00:17:32.868 --> 00:17:35.771
You went through Resonance with Kazuki.

00:17:35.771 --> 00:17:38.507
So why won't you do what Kazuki tells you?

00:17:38.507 --> 00:17:41.610
I am who I am!
I don't take orders from anyone.

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:43.712
How is it that you're free?

00:17:43.712 --> 00:17:45.339
Who knows?

00:17:50.686 --> 00:17:52.788
I find you quite interesting.

00:17:52.788 --> 00:17:55.188
I'm not interested in you!

00:18:12.775 --> 00:18:14.265
Machina!

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:11.800
I want to know the truth!
That's why I'm going to go see Toa.

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:13.825
See her, and find out for sure!

00:19:15.471 --> 00:19:17.973
We don't have to go after them.

00:19:17.973 --> 00:19:21.276
They might be able to alter it.

00:19:21.276 --> 00:19:23.107
Alter?

00:19:24.313 --> 00:19:28.181
Mm-hmm, the Dragon-human relationship.

00:19:29.318 --> 00:19:31.720
Picking up G-10's Actualization reading

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:34.323
in the sky over the sea near Shin-Ogasawara.

00:19:34.323 --> 00:19:39.795
Currently at Point Alpha-12,
rising at 2 kilometers per second.

00:19:39.795 --> 00:19:42.127
So that's Gio, huh?

00:19:48.303 --> 00:19:51.173
G-10 is about to leave the stratosphere.

00:19:51.173 --> 00:19:54.576
We can no longer follow him on radar.

00:19:54.576 --> 00:19:57.579
G-10 lost.

00:19:57.579 --> 00:20:01.517
Judging from his direction,
he's headed for the Moon.

00:20:01.517 --> 00:20:04.975
Prepare a spaceship at once.
I'm going after him!

00:20:10.359 --> 00:20:14.563
That rotten Jin, he's taken my Gio again.

00:20:14.563 --> 00:20:17.099
He'll pay for this, I swear!

00:20:17.099 --> 00:20:19.568
Well, well, it's the Dragonaut rookie hopeful,

00:20:19.568 --> 00:20:22.204
who had his Dragon stolen from him.

00:20:22.204 --> 00:20:25.574
Are you sure you should be
wasting your time in here?

00:20:25.574 --> 00:20:28.444
You never know when the
order might come to deploy.

00:20:28.444 --> 00:20:32.175
Although, how can you
deploy without your ride?

00:20:41.223 --> 00:20:44.927
The beauty of Earth when
seen from space, particularly.

00:20:44.927 --> 00:20:47.691
You could say it's life-changing.

00:21:03.812 --> 00:21:07.077
So that's... Earth...

00:22:07.476 --> 00:22:14.149
Me to me ga atta shunkan

00:22:14.149 --> 00:22:20.956
kanashimi ga hajimaru ki ga shita

00:22:20.956 --> 00:22:27.629
Keshite mo kienai kioku ima demo

00:22:27.629 --> 00:22:34.831
futari no kokoro tsunaide'ru

00:22:36.672 --> 00:22:43.512
Ikusen no hoshi no kazu hodo hito wa

00:22:43.512 --> 00:22:46.515
afurete iru no ni ne

00:22:46.515 --> 00:22:50.385
kimi shika mienai

00:22:50.385 --> 00:22:53.555
Aenakute mo

00:22:53.555 --> 00:22:56.491
kanawanakute mo

00:22:56.491 --> 00:23:02.764
tsunoru omoi wa kitto eien

00:23:02.764 --> 00:23:09.771
Unmei ga futari wo hikisaku nara

00:23:09.771 --> 00:23:16.612
deaeta koto dake wo kiseki to shinjite

00:23:16.612 --> 00:23:23.218
Hora nagarete'ku kono ame no you

00:23:23.218 --> 00:23:29.258
Itoshisa dake wo kimi ni furasetai

00:23:29.258 --> 00:23:33.456
Rain of Love

00:23:43.372 --> 00:23:44.706
Ready, set...

00:23:44.706 --> 00:23:46.642
We're your ISDA operators,

00:23:46.642 --> 00:23:47.909
- Saki!
- Ryoko!
- Megumi!

00:23:47.909 --> 00:23:50.379
Hey, the most important part
got all messed up, didn't it?

00:23:50.379 --> 00:23:52.047
Ryoko-san, you said we
should all say them together

00:23:52.047 --> 00:23:53.315
so there wouldn't be any arguing.

00:23:53.315 --> 00:23:55.317
Oh, yeah? Well, you agreed to it, didn't you?

00:23:55.317 --> 00:23:58.787
Now, now, don't argue about it.
Next time, we'll do it better.

00:23:58.787 --> 00:24:01.123
Next time? We have to do the preview!

00:24:01.123 --> 00:24:03.592
Right! Okay then, I'll do it! Let's see...

00:24:03.592 --> 00:24:05.927
Next time, all sorts of people
will come attacking!

00:24:05.927 --> 00:24:08.487
- Aw, you took it from me.
- How inconsiderate!
